course: dictionary
lesson: 11089
title: Whack in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word whack has several meanings, so the words around it tell you which one is meant. Look for clues such as a ball, a bat, a share of money or the word tired. «Lily has never played rounders; she misses five times, then whacks the ball into the duck pond.» Whacks means hits hard, because she is swinging a bat at a ball.
explain: «A tuskfish has no hands, so it carries a clam in its mouth and whacks it on a rock until it cracks.» Here whacks still means hits hard, but the hitting is done to crack a shell. Ask yourself: what is being hit, and why?
explain: Some uses are informal, like «I'm whacked» or «out of whack». The clues are your friends here: whacked means very tired, and out of whack means not working properly. Hitting people is never okay, so a whack is always a hit on a ball, a nail or a piñata, not a person.
fact: Whack can be a verb, a noun or an adjective.
fact: «Whack» means to hit something hard, often with a stick or a hand.
fact: «A whack» can be a hard hit, or the sound of one.
fact: «Have a whack at it» means have a try, and «pay your whack» means pay your share.
fact: «Out of whack» means not working properly, and «I'm whacked» means I'm very tired.
exercise: «Lily whacks the ball into the duck pond.» What does whacks mean here? | *Hits hard | Carefully lifts | Counts | Kicks softly
exercise: Sam says, «I'll have a whack at the puzzle.» What does he mean? | He will hit the puzzle | *He will try the puzzle | He will give up on the puzzle | He will pay for the puzzle
exercise: «The machine is out of whack, so it keeps beeping.» What does out of whack suggest? | Full of cake | Very quiet | *Not working properly | Brand new and shiny
test: «A tuskfish whacks a clam on a rock until it cracks.» Why does the tuskfish whack the clam? | *To crack the shell open | To wash it | To make music | To put it to sleep
test: Mia's dad says, «I'm whacked after work.» What does whacked mean? | Very happy | *Very tired | Very hungry | Very hit
exam: In «He whacks the nail into the wood», which word means the same as whacks? | forgets | sleeps | *hammers | sings
